<WidgetStyles>
<!--
    Generated by tools/roundrect.py - do not hand-edit, edit the generator and re-run it.

    round_* are the border-radius patches: an Edge panel with a Fill panel inset 1 px inside
    it is one rounded, bordered box. Radius 5 standard, 4 _sm, 3 _xs, 2 _dot.

    They are declared three times over, for PanelWidget, WrapSpacerWidget and GridSpacerWidget,
    because a style block is per widget CLASS and a spacer cannot wear a radius declared for
    PanelWidget. The three blocks are the same styles off the same sprites - a spacer that lays
    its children out and paints its own rounded background needs no panel behind it. (The
    _dash outlines are PanelWidget-only: they are size-specific to the garage's empty slots.)

    The ButtonWidget styles are the interactive-state component. Normal draws nothing, so a
    widget keeps whatever resting look its Edge+Fill host already has; Disabled always lays a
    black wash over it. Highlight and Pushed depend on the tier - a BUTTON lightens, a ROW
    darkens. Sprites are tinted by the widget colour:

        style row
        color 1 1 1 1           <- REQUIRED. color 0 0 0 0 multiplies every state to nothing.

    Hue is never in a sprite. Tint a BUTTON with an accent and its white wash becomes that
    colour, which is what lets one sprite serve all six runtime-selectable accents. A row's wash
    is black and so is accent-invariant: RGB 0 survives any multiply.

    Radius follows the panel ladder - no suffix r5, _sm r4, _xs r3, flat r1 - and must match the
    panel underneath, not the widget's importance. Two strength tiers, pulling opposite ways:

      button tier   WHITE 0.11 / 0.16 (primary, accent and danger stronger). A control the eye
                    expects to light up.
                    btn_primary r5   btn_accent r5   btn_danger r5
                    btn_quiet r5     btn_quiet_sm r4  btn_quiet_xs r3
                    btn_icon r4      btn_icon_xs r3
                    chip r5          chip_sm r4
      row tier      BLACK 0.30 hover / 0.42 press (was white 0.055 / 0.09 until 2026-09-20). The
                    white version read as loud as a SELECTED row - +13 on #121212 against
                    selection's +15 - and lightening the ground under light text is what put
                    Steel, Rust/Danger and Tritanopia-Danger labels under WCAG AA while hovered.
                    Darkening moves the opposite way from selection and raises every ratio.
                    Press stops at 0.42 so it never out-darks Disabled (0.42 / 0.45).
                    toggle r5        card r5          card_sm r4
                    tab r1           row r1
      no paint      hit              a hit area that must stay invisible

    round_fill_grad is the item-rarity wash: the same rounded rect with its alpha ramping from
    15 % at the top down to full at the bottom. It is 64 x 64 rather than 11 x 11 because a nine-slice
    flattens anything drawn along the axis it stretches, so the ramp has to live in the centre
    cell at roughly the size it is used - see the note on grad_patch in the generator.

    round_edge_dash / _sm are dashed 1 px outlines for the garage's empty slots. Unlike every
    other style here they are SIZE-SPECIFIC, because a dash cannot survive a nine-slice edge cell
    (1 px in the direction it stretches) and the engine has no tiling property. Use each at its
    intended size; the widget colour is the line colour, as with round_edge.

      round_edge_dash     383 x 62  the empty-slot tile (left column is a fixed 520 design px)
      round_edge_dash_sm   56 x 56  the empty-garage panel's icon box
-->
    <Widget Name="PanelWidget">
        <Style Name="round_fill" Font="" ImageSet="Rounded" Color="4294967295">
            <State Name="Normal">
                <Item Name="LeftTop" Image="Fill5_LT" />
                <Item Name="Top" Image="Fill5_T" />
                <Item Name="RightTop" Image="Fill5_RT" />
                <Item Name="Right" Image="Fill5_R" />
                <Item Name="RightBottom" Image="Fill5_RB" />
                <Item Name="Bottom" Image="Fill5_B" />
                <Item Name="LeftBottom" Image="Fill5_LB" />
                <Item Name="Center" Image="Fill5_C" />
                <Item Name="Left" Image="Fill5_L" />
            </State>
            <State Name="Disabled">
                <Item Name="LeftTop" Image="Fill5_LT" />
                <Item Name="Top" Image="Fill5_T" />
                <Item Name="RightTop" Image="Fill5_RT" />
                <Item Name="Right" Image="Fill5_R" />
                <Item Name="RightBottom" Image="Fill5_RB" />
                <Item Name="Bottom" Image="Fill5_B" />
                <Item Name="LeftBottom" Image="Fill5_LB" />
